    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nadditional Judge means a Judge appointed under subsection (2) of\nsection 7;\ncause includes any suit, and also includes criminal proceedings;\nChief Justice means the Chief Justice of the Court, and includes a\nJudge for the time being performing the duties and exercising the\npowers of the Chief Justice;\ndefendant includes any person against whom any relief is sought in\na matter or who is required to attend the proceedings in a matter as\na party thereto;\nDeputy Registrar means a Deputy Registrar of the Supreme Court;\nDeputy Sheriff means a Deputy Sheriff of the Territory;\nenactment has the same meaning as in section 3 of the Australian\nCapital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988;",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act, unless the contrary intention appears:\nadditional Judge means a Judge appointed under subsection (2) of\nsection 7;\ncause includes any suit, and also includes criminal proceedings;\nChief Justice means the Chief Justice of the Court, and includes a\nJudge for the time being performing the duties and exercising the\npowers of the Chief Justice;\ndefendant includes any person against whom any relief is sought in\na matter or who is required to attend the proceedings in a matter as\na party thereto;\nDeputy Registrar means a Deputy Registrar of the Supreme Court;\nDeputy Sheriff means a Deputy Sheriff of the Territory;\nenactment has the same meaning as in section 3 of the Australian\nCapital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-5-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
