    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-7-ss-1b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7(1B) Appointment and tenure of Judges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-7-ss-1b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1B) The Chief Justice is the senior Judge of the Court and the other\nJudges appointed under subsection (1) have seniority as between\nthemselves according to the dates on which their commissions took\neffect or, where the commissions of 2 or more of them took effect\non the same date, according to the precedence assigned to them by\ntheir commissions, and Judges appointed under subsection (1) are\nsenior to the additional Judges.",
      "skos:definition": "(1B) The Chief Justice is the senior Judge of the Court and the other\nJudges appointed under subsection (1) have seniority as between\nthemselves according to the dates on which their commissions took\neffect or, where the commissions of 2 or more of them took effect\non the same date, according to the precedence assigned to them by\ntheir commissions, and Judges appointed under subsection (1) are\nsenior to the additional Judges.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-7"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-7-ss-1b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-7-ss-1b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ff3ab9500b57a19b7104924def46cc7c8bbda1880ee104df10cba7376c9d591",
      "skos:note": "Judges have seniority based on commission dates."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-7-ss-1b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7(1B) Appointment and tenure of Judges",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1B) The Chief Justice is the senior Judge of the Court and the other\nJudges appointed under subsection (1) have seniority as between\nthemselves according to the dates on which their commissions took\neffect or, where the commissions of 2 or more of them took effect\non the same date, according to the precedence assigned to them by\ntheir commissions, and Judges appointed under subsection (1) are\nsenior to the additional Judges."
    },
