      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where the jurisdiction of the Court is to be, or is being, exercised\nin a particular case by the Master:\n\n(a) the Master may, on the Master’s own motion or on the\napplication of a party to the proceedings, refer the\nproceedings to the Court constituted by one Judge; and\n\n(b) a Judge may, on the application of a party to the proceedings,\nat any time before the conclusion of the proceedings before\nthe Master, order that the jurisdiction of the Court in the case\nbe exercised by the Court constituted by one Judge.\n\n(2) Where, under subsection (1), proceedings are referred or removed\nto the Court constituted by one Judge, the Court may:\n\n(a) give such directions as it considers appropriate as to the\nprocedure to be followed in the further conduct of the\nproceedings, including, in a case where evidence was\n\n\nConstitution and Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court  Part II\n\nSection 8A\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933\n\nrecorded before the referral or removal, directions as to the\nuse (if any) to be made of the evidence; and\n\n(b) remit the proceedings to the Master with such directions as\nthe Court considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where the jurisdiction of the Court is to be, or is being, exercised\nin a particular case by the Master:\n\n(a) the Master may, on the Master’s own motion or on the\napplication of a party to the proceedings, refer the\nproceedings to the Court constituted by one Judge; and\n\n(b) a Judge may, on the application of a party to the proceedings,\nat any time before the conclusion of the proceedings before\nthe Master, order that the jurisdiction of the Court in the case\nbe exercised by the Court constituted by one Judge.\n\n(2) Where, under subsection (1), proceedings are referred or removed\nto the Court constituted by one Judge, the Court may:\n\n(a) give such directions as it considers appropriate as to the\nprocedure to be followed in the further conduct of the\nproceedings, including, in a case where evidence was\n\n\nConstitution and Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court  Part II\n\nSection 8A\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933\n\nrecorded before the referral or removal, directions as to the\nuse (if any) to be made of the evidence; and\n\n(b) remit the proceedings to the Master with such directions as\nthe Court considers appropriate.",
