    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-8b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8B(5) Salary and allowances of Judges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-8b-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subject to subsection (6), a person who holds office as a Judge of\nthe Court by virtue of an appointment that took effect while he was\na Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the Federal Court of\nAustralia is not, while he continues to hold office both as a Judge\nof the Court and as a Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the\nFederal Court of Australia, entitled to receive salary or annual\nallowance as provided in subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Subject to subsection (6), a person who holds office as a Judge of\nthe Court by virtue of an appointment that took effect while he was\na Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the Federal Court of\nAustralia is not, while he continues to hold office both as a Judge\nof the Court and as a Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the\nFederal Court of Australia, entitled to receive salary or annual\nallowance as provided in subsection (1).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-8b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-8b-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-8b-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4167c3b3cdfd8a039a2f6d2300863233da1534fbc1de32bf74c48af18ebcbd01",
      "skos:note": "No salary or allowance for judges appointed before a certain date."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-8b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8B(5) Salary and allowances of Judges",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subject to subsection (6), a person who holds office as a Judge of\nthe Court by virtue of an appointment that took effect while he was\na Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the Federal Court of\nAustralia is not, while he continues to hold office both as a Judge\nof the Court and as a Judge (including the Chief Judge) of the\nFederal Court of Australia, entitled to receive salary or annual\nallowance as provided in subsection (1)."
    },
