    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Jurisdiction of Supreme Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "The Supreme Court:\n\n(a) has, subject to this or any other Act or to any Ordinance or\nenactment, in relation to the Territory, the same original\njurisdiction, both civil and criminal, as the Supreme Court of\nthe State of New South Wales had in relation to that State\nimmediately before 1 January 1911;\n\n(b) has such jurisdiction, both civil and criminal, and whether\noriginal or otherwise, as is from time to time vested in the\nSupreme Court by Act, by Ordinance or by enactment; and\n\n(c) has jurisdiction, with such exceptions and subject to such\nconditions as are provided by Act or by Ordinance or\nenactment, to hear and determine appeals from all judgments,\nconvictions, orders and sentences of inferior courts having\njurisdiction in the Territory.\n\nNote: The Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory has jurisdiction in the\nAustralian Antarctic Territory and in Heard Island and McDonald Islands; see\nsection 10 of the Australian Antarctic Territory Act 1954 and section 9 of the Heard\nIsland and McDonald Islands Act 1953.",
      "skos:definition": "The Supreme Court:\n\n(a) has, subject to this or any other Act or to any Ordinance or\nenactment, in relation to the Territory, the same original\njurisdiction, both civil and criminal, as the Supreme Court of\nthe State of New South Wales had in relation to that State\nimmediately before 1 January 1911;\n\n(b) has such jurisdiction, both civil and criminal, and whether\noriginal or otherwise, as is from time to time vested in the\nSupreme Court by Act, by Ordinance or by enactment; and\n\n(c) has jurisdiction, with such exceptions and subject to such\nconditions as are provided by Act or by Ordinance or\nenactment, to hear and determine appeals from all judgments,\nconvictions, orders and sentences of inferior courts having\njurisdiction in the Territory.\n\nNote: The Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory has jurisdiction in the\nAustralian Antarctic Territory and in Heard Island and McDonald Islands; see\nsection 10 of the Australian Antarctic Territory Act 1954 and section 9 of the Heard\nIsland and McDonald Islands Act 1953.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-11-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fe9b640289575391d0d49c8ea2bb26b7166cc3263fff54ed8d968dff1bdd74dd",
      "skos:note": "Supreme Court has jurisdiction over the Territory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Jurisdiction of Supreme Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "The Supreme Court:\n\n(a) has, subject to this or any other Act or to any Ordinance or\nenactment, in relation to the Territory, the same original\njurisdiction, both civil and criminal, as the Supreme Court of\nthe State of New South Wales had in relation to that State\nimmediately before 1 January 1911;\n\n(b) has such jurisdiction, both civil and criminal, and whether\noriginal or otherwise, as is from time to time vested in the\nSupreme Court by Act, by Ordinance or by enactment; and\n\n(c) has jurisdiction, with such exceptions and subject to such\nconditions as are provided by Act or by Ordinance or\nenactment, to hear and determine appeals from all judgments,\nconvictions, orders and sentences of inferior courts having\njurisdiction in the Territory.\n\nNote: The Supreme Court of the Australian Capital Territory has jurisdiction in the\nAustralian Antarctic Territory and in Heard Island and McDonald Islands; see\nsection 10 of the Australian Antarctic Territory Act 1954 and section 9 of the Heard\nIsland and McDonald Islands Act 1953."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-11-norm",
