      "values:originalText": "(1) The jurisdiction of the Supreme Court that is exercisable by one\nJudge may be exercised by the Judge sitting in Chambers, in the\nfollowing cases:\n\n(a) Applications relating to the conduct of a cause or matter;\n\n(b) Applications relating to the custody, management or\npreservation of property, or to the sale of property and the\ndisposition of the purchase money;\n\n(c) Applications which, by the terms of any law of the State of\nNew South Wales continued in force in the Territory, may be\nmade to a Judge of the Supreme Court of New South Wales\nsitting in Chambers; and\n\n(d) Applications for directions and other applications which, by\nor under this, or any other Act, by or under an Ordinance or\nenactment or by Rules of Court, are authorized to be made to\nthe Judge sitting in Chambers;"
