    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "27 Practice and procedure",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-27"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and\nprocedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other\nAct, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter\nshall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and\nprocedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice\nand procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as\nnearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme\nCourt of New South Wales.",
      "skos:definition": "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and\nprocedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other\nAct, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter\nshall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and\nprocedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice\nand procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as\nnearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme\nCourt of New South Wales.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "06c2f05a97427e164fc6c35b9b6383e206ae8e23580c01b7ba3c59c062161b7b",
      "skos:note": "Governs practice and procedure of Supreme Court by High Court or Supreme Court of New South Wales"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-27",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "27 Practice and procedure",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and\nprocedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other\nAct, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter\nshall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and\nprocedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice\nand procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as\nnearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme\nCourt of New South Wales."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Rules of Court",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Judges appointed under subsection (1) of section 7 or any two\nof those Judges may make Rules of Court, not inconsistent with\nthis or any other Act, with regulations under this or any other Act\nor with any Ordinance:\n\n(a) for regulating and prescribing:\n\n(i) the practice and procedure, including the method of\npleading, to be followed in the Supreme Court and in\nthe offices of the Court; and\n\n(ii) all matters and things incidental to or relating to any\nsuch practice and procedure or necessary or convenient\nto be prescribed for the conduct of any business of the\nCourt;\n\n(b) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by any law of the\nCommonwealth or of the Territory that makes provision for\nthe incorporation of, and otherwise in relation to, companies,\nrequired or permitted to be prescribed by regulation under\nthat law;\n\n(c) for prescribing the qualifications for the admission of persons\nto practise as barristers and solicitors of the Supreme Court;\nand\n\n(d) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by this Act or by\nany Ordinance or enactment, required or permitted to be\nprescribed by Rules of Court.\n\n(2) In particular the Rules of Court may provide:\n\n(a) for the places of sitting of the Court;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Judges appointed under subsection (1) of section 7 or any two\nof those Judges may make Rules of Court, not inconsistent with\nthis or any other Act, with regulations under this or any other Act\nor with any Ordinance:\n\n(a) for regulating and prescribing:\n\n(i) the practice and procedure, including the method of\npleading, to be followed in the Supreme Court and in\nthe offices of the Court; and\n\n(ii) all matters and things incidental to or relating to any\nsuch practice and procedure or necessary or convenient\nto be prescribed for the conduct of any business of the\nCourt;\n\n(b) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by any law of the\nCommonwealth or of the Territory that makes provision for\nthe incorporation of, and otherwise in relation to, companies,\nrequired or permitted to be prescribed by regulation under\nthat law;\n\n(c) for prescribing the qualifications for the admission of persons\nto practise as barristers and solicitors of the Supreme Court;\nand\n\n(d) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by this Act or by\nany Ordinance or enactment, required or permitted to be\nprescribed by Rules of Court.\n\n(2) In particular the Rules of Court may provide:\n\n(a) for the places of sitting of the Court;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4090702bbec3d23ce230db38bc3c4b748779c9e58f0e8e7aab1c0f488a0b8a1f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Rules of Court",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Judges appointed under subsection (1) of section 7 or any two\nof those Judges may make Rules of Court, not inconsistent with\nthis or any other Act, with regulations under this or any other Act\nor with any Ordinance:\n\n(a) for regulating and prescribing:\n\n(i) the practice and procedure, including the method of\npleading, to be followed in the Supreme Court and in\nthe offices of the Court; and\n\n(ii) all matters and things incidental to or relating to any\nsuch practice and procedure or necessary or convenient\nto be prescribed for the conduct of any business of the\nCourt;\n\n(b) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by any law of the\nCommonwealth or of the Territory that makes provision for\nthe incorporation of, and otherwise in relation to, companies,\nrequired or permitted to be prescribed by regulation under\nthat law;\n\n(c) for prescribing the qualifications for the admission of persons\nto practise as barristers and solicitors of the Supreme Court;\nand\n\n(d) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by this Act or by\nany Ordinance or enactment, required or permitted to be\nprescribed by Rules of Court.\n\n(2) In particular the Rules of Court may provide:\n\n(a) for the places of sitting of the Court;"
    },
