    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Powers and duties of Master",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Master has power to administer oaths, and may exercise such\nother powers, and shall perform such duties, as are assigned to the\nMaster by or under an Act, Ordinance or enactment, by Rules of\nCourt or by a special order of the court.\n\n(2) Where, under a law of New South Wales that is continued in force\nin the Territory as a law of the Territory, a power is exercisable, or\na duty is to be performed, or a thing is to be done, by the Master in\nEquity, it may be exercised, performed or done by:\n\n(a) the Master; or\n\n(b) at a time when there is no Master, the Registrar.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Master has power to administer oaths, and may exercise such\nother powers, and shall perform such duties, as are assigned to the\nMaster by or under an Act, Ordinance or enactment, by Rules of\nCourt or by a special order of the court.\n\n(2) Where, under a law of New South Wales that is continued in force\nin the Territory as a law of the Territory, a power is exercisable, or\na duty is to be performed, or a thing is to be done, by the Master in\nEquity, it may be exercised, performed or done by:\n\n(a) the Master; or\n\n(b) at a time when there is no Master, the Registrar.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-31-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07952856a2f62df52a879107e472f9427b61fefbd0c2f2fdf7aae305093a0486"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Powers and duties of Master",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Master has power to administer oaths, and may exercise such\nother powers, and shall perform such duties, as are assigned to the\nMaster by or under an Act, Ordinance or enactment, by Rules of\nCourt or by a special order of the court.\n\n(2) Where, under a law of New South Wales that is continued in force\nin the Territory as a law of the Territory, a power is exercisable, or\na duty is to be performed, or a thing is to be done, by the Master in\nEquity, it may be exercised, performed or done by:\n\n(a) the Master; or\n\n(b) at a time when there is no Master, the Registrar."
    },
