      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Master shall be appointed by the Governor-General.\n\n(2) A person shall not be appointed as the Master unless the person has\nbeen enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court or of the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory for not less than 5 years.\n\n(3) A person who has attained 65 years of age shall not be appointed\nas the Master.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Master shall be appointed by the Governor-General.\n\n(2) A person shall not be appointed as the Master unless the person has\nbeen enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court or of the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory for not less than 5 years.\n\n(3) A person who has attained 65 years of age shall not be appointed\nas the Master.",
