    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33F Acting appointments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-33f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may appoint a person who is eligible to be\nappointed as Master to act as the Master:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Master (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period when the Master is absent from duty or\nfrom Australia or is, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe duties of the office.\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as Master shall not continue to act for\nmore than 12 months.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) a person is acting under paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) the office of Master becomes vacant;\nthen, subject to subsection (2), the person may continue to act until\nthe vacancy is filled.\n\n(4) A person acting as Master has all the powers and duties of the\nMaster, and the laws of the Commonwealth and the Territory\n(including this Act and the Rules of Court) apply in relation to the\nperson as if the person were the Master.\n\n(5) The Minister may determine the terms and conditions of\nappointment, including remuneration and allowances, of a person\nacting as Master.\n\n(6) A person acting as Master may be removed or suspended from\noffice only under section 33D.\n\n(7) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act as\nMaster is not invalid because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen;\n\n\nThe Master  Part III\n\nSection 33F\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Governor-General may appoint a person who is eligible to be\nappointed as Master to act as the Master:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Master (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period when the Master is absent from duty or\nfrom Australia or is, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe duties of the office.\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as Master shall not continue to act for\nmore than 12 months.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) a person is acting under paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) the office of Master becomes vacant;\nthen, subject to subsection (2), the person may continue to act until\nthe vacancy is filled.\n\n(4) A person acting as Master has all the powers and duties of the\nMaster, and the laws of the Commonwealth and the Territory\n(including this Act and the Rules of Court) apply in relation to the\nperson as if the person were the Master.\n\n(5) The Minister may determine the terms and conditions of\nappointment, including remuneration and allowances, of a person\nacting as Master.\n\n(6) A person acting as Master may be removed or suspended from\noffice only under section 33D.\n\n(7) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act as\nMaster is not invalid because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen;\n\n\nThe Master  Part III\n\nSection 33F\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-33f-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dfd85ec6c5a89417f4e522e87a1511f4520456a6e66842737b81491ffe7e8d94"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-33f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33F Acting appointments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Governor-General may appoint a person who is eligible to be\nappointed as Master to act as the Master:\n\n(a) during a vacancy in the office of Master (whether or not an\nappointment has previously been made to the office); or\n\n(b) during any period when the Master is absent from duty or\nfrom Australia or is, for any other reason, unable to perform\nthe duties of the office.\n\n(2) A person appointed to act as Master shall not continue to act for\nmore than 12 months.\n\n(3) Where:\n\n(a) a person is acting under paragraph (1)(b); and\n\n(b) the office of Master becomes vacant;\nthen, subject to subsection (2), the person may continue to act until\nthe vacancy is filled.\n\n(4) A person acting as Master has all the powers and duties of the\nMaster, and the laws of the Commonwealth and the Territory\n(including this Act and the Rules of Court) apply in relation to the\nperson as if the person were the Master.\n\n(5) The Minister may determine the terms and conditions of\nappointment, including remuneration and allowances, of a person\nacting as Master.\n\n(6) A person acting as Master may be removed or suspended from\noffice only under section 33D.\n\n(7) Anything done by or in relation to a person purporting to act as\nMaster is not invalid because:\n\n(a) the occasion for the appointment had not arisen;\n\n\nThe Master  Part III\n\nSection 33F\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933\n\n(b) there was a defect or irregularity in connection with the\nappointment; or\n\n(c) the appointment had ceased to have effect."
    },
