      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Registrar has power to administer oaths, and may exercise\nsuch other powers, and shall perform such duties, as are assigned\nto him by or under any Act or Ordinance, by enactment, by Rules\nof Court or by a special order of the Court.\n\n(2) Where, under a law of the State of New South Wales which is\ncontinued in force in the Territory as a law of the Territory, a\npower is exercisable, or a duty is to be performed, or a thing is to\nbe done, by the Prothonotary or a Registrar, it may be exercised,\nperformed or done by the Registrar.\n\n\nOfficers  Part IV\n\nSection 35A\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933",
