    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-35-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35(2) Powers and duties of Registrar",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where, under a law of the State of New South Wales which is\ncontinued in force in the Territory as a law of the Territory, a\npower is exercisable, or a duty is to be performed, or a thing is to\nbe done, by the Prothonotary or a Registrar, it may be exercised,\nperformed or done by the Registrar.\n\n\nOfficers  Part IV\n\nSection 35A\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-35-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
