      "cml:conclusionText": "Registrar may exercise power"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-35a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "35A Proceedings before Registrar in relation to winding-up of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-35a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "companies\n\n(1) The Supreme Court, in making an order for the winding-up of a\ncompany, may direct that all proceedings for and in relation to the\nwinding-up shall be had and taken before the Master or Registrar.\n\n(2) Where the Court gives a direction under the last preceding\nsubsection in relation to the winding-up of a company:\n\n(a) the Master or Registrar, as the case requires, has, in relation\nto the winding-up, all the powers of the Court;\n\n(b) the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, may refer to the\nCourt any matter in relation to the winding-up that he thinks\nproper to be determined by the Court; and\n\n(c) an appeal lies to the Court from any order, decree or direction\nof the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, made or given\nin relation to the winding-up.\n\n(3) In this section, ‘the Registrar’ does not include a Deputy Registrar.",
      "skos:definition": "companies\n\n(1) The Supreme Court, in making an order for the winding-up of a\ncompany, may direct that all proceedings for and in relation to the\nwinding-up shall be had and taken before the Master or Registrar.\n\n(2) Where the Court gives a direction under the last preceding\nsubsection in relation to the winding-up of a company:\n\n(a) the Master or Registrar, as the case requires, has, in relation\nto the winding-up, all the powers of the Court;\n\n(b) the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, may refer to the\nCourt any matter in relation to the winding-up that he thinks\nproper to be determined by the Court; and\n\n(c) an appeal lies to the Court from any order, decree or direction\nof the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, made or given\nin relation to the winding-up.\n\n(3) In this section, ‘the Registrar’ does not include a Deputy Registrar.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-35a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-35a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-35a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1701cfb023a18b1534d60983d25660944bf18c8928d27c2658306664990bc734"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-35a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35A Proceedings before Registrar in relation to winding-up of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "companies\n\n(1) The Supreme Court, in making an order for the winding-up of a\ncompany, may direct that all proceedings for and in relation to the\nwinding-up shall be had and taken before the Master or Registrar.\n\n(2) Where the Court gives a direction under the last preceding\nsubsection in relation to the winding-up of a company:\n\n(a) the Master or Registrar, as the case requires, has, in relation\nto the winding-up, all the powers of the Court;\n\n(b) the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, may refer to the\nCourt any matter in relation to the winding-up that he thinks\nproper to be determined by the Court; and\n\n(c) an appeal lies to the Court from any order, decree or direction\nof the Master or Registrar, as the case may be, made or given\nin relation to the winding-up.\n\n(3) In this section, ‘the Registrar’ does not include a Deputy Registrar."
    },
