    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-37a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "37A Deputy Sheriffs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-37a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.32",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to the directions of the Sheriff, a Deputy Sheriff has, and\nmay exercise and perform, all the powers and functions of the\nSheriff under this or any other Act, an Ordinance, enactment or\nRules of Court, and, in exercising or performing those powers and\nfunctions, has the same rights, privileges, immunities, duties and\nliabilities as the Sheriff.\n\n(2) The appointment of a person to be a Deputy Sheriff does not affect\nthe exercise or performance of a power or function by the Sheriff.\n\n\nGeneral Matters of Procedure  Part V\n\nSection 38\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to the directions of the Sheriff, a Deputy Sheriff has, and\nmay exercise and perform, all the powers and functions of the\nSheriff under this or any other Act, an Ordinance, enactment or\nRules of Court, and, in exercising or performing those powers and\nfunctions, has the same rights, privileges, immunities, duties and\nliabilities as the Sheriff.\n\n(2) The appointment of a person to be a Deputy Sheriff does not affect\nthe exercise or performance of a power or function by the Sheriff.\n\n\nGeneral Matters of Procedure  Part V\n\nSection 38\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-37a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-37a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "561636ffae04a80e6e34c0cd4ef4a3066b61f877a562c550a1e003e842f9c922"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-37a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "37A Deputy Sheriffs",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 32,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to the directions of the Sheriff, a Deputy Sheriff has, and\nmay exercise and perform, all the powers and functions of the\nSheriff under this or any other Act, an Ordinance, enactment or\nRules of Court, and, in exercising or performing those powers and\nfunctions, has the same rights, privileges, immunities, duties and\nliabilities as the Sheriff.\n\n(2) The appointment of a person to be a Deputy Sheriff does not affect\nthe exercise or performance of a power or function by the Sheriff.\n\n\nGeneral Matters of Procedure  Part V\n\nSection 38\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933"
    },
