    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "38 Manner of giving evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-38"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "Except as otherwise provided by this Act by an Ordinance or by an\nenactment, or unless in any suit the parties agree to the contrary,\nevidence in any matter shall be given orally in open court.",
      "skos:definition": "Except as otherwise provided by this Act by an Ordinance or by an\nenactment, or unless in any suit the parties agree to the contrary,\nevidence in any matter shall be given orally in open court.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "71a46fb66c2d8dd63e3f6e7d3818633e0b60e4b5a858433da26d2881fb36e2eb",
      "skos:note": "Oral evidence is required in open court, unless parties agree otherwise."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-38",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "38 Manner of giving evidence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "Except as otherwise provided by this Act by an Ordinance or by an\nenactment, or unless in any suit the parties agree to the contrary,\nevidence in any matter shall be given orally in open court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-38-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "requires",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Requires oral evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-39",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "39 Evidence by affidavit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-39"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) On the hearing of any matter, evidence may be given by affidavit\nof the service of any document incidental to the proceedings in the\nmatter or of the signature of a party to the matter, or of his\nsolicitor, to such a document.\n\n(2) On or before the hearing of a civil matter, the Court or a Judge\nmay, for sufficient reason, order that all or a part of the evidence in\nthe matter, being evidence that but for the order would be required\nto be given orally in open court, may be given by affidavit.\n\n(3) An order under the last preceding subsection may be made subject\nto such conditions as the Court or Judge thinks just.\n\n(4) The conditions referred to in the last preceding subsection may\ninclude a condition that copies of an affidavit by which any\nevidence is given be served on a party or parties to the matter and a\ncondition that a person whose evidence is given by affidavit attend\nat the hearing for cross examination.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) On the hearing of any matter, evidence may be given by affidavit\nof the service of any document incidental to the proceedings in the\nmatter or of the signature of a party to the matter, or of his\nsolicitor, to such a document.\n\n(2) On or before the hearing of a civil matter, the Court or a Judge\nmay, for sufficient reason, order that all or a part of the evidence in\nthe matter, being evidence that but for the order would be required\nto be given orally in open court, may be given by affidavit.\n\n(3) An order under the last preceding subsection may be made subject\nto such conditions as the Court or Judge thinks just.\n\n(4) The conditions referred to in the last preceding subsection may\ninclude a condition that copies of an affidavit by which any\nevidence is given be served on a party or parties to the matter and a\ncondition that a person whose evidence is given by affidavit attend\nat the hearing for cross examination.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-39-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-39-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-39-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-39-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0fbf102fda04ddcab523dafb075e8a9c2698130f102e46f4478378e2604c3538"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-39",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39 Evidence by affidavit",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1) On the hearing of any matter, evidence may be given by affidavit\nof the service of any document incidental to the proceedings in the\nmatter or of the signature of a party to the matter, or of his\nsolicitor, to such a document.\n\n(2) On or before the hearing of a civil matter, the Court or a Judge\nmay, for sufficient reason, order that all or a part of the evidence in\nthe matter, being evidence that but for the order would be required\nto be given orally in open court, may be given by affidavit.\n\n(3) An order under the last preceding subsection may be made subject\nto such conditions as the Court or Judge thinks just.\n\n(4) The conditions referred to in the last preceding subsection may\ninclude a condition that copies of an affidavit by which any\nevidence is given be served on a party or parties to the matter and a\ncondition that a person whose evidence is given by affidavit attend\nat the hearing for cross examination."
    },
