    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-53-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53(4) Indictable offences",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-53-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where a person has been committed for trial upon a charge for an\nindictable offence triable before the Supreme Court, the\ninformation against the person may include, either in substitution\nfor, or in addition to, a count charging the offence for which he\nwas committed, a count founded on a fact or evidence disclosed in\nthe course of the committal proceedings.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where a person has been committed for trial upon a charge for an\nindictable offence triable before the Supreme Court, the\ninformation against the person may include, either in substitution\nfor, or in addition to, a count charging the offence for which he\nwas committed, a count founded on a fact or evidence disclosed in\nthe course of the committal proceedings.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-53"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-53-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-53-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f90e5bfcd78cc731ec8917c8ad589e3e82ead93f0d82dea13a80b3133728a205",
      "skos:note": "Information against a person charged with an indictable offence may include additional counts based on evidence from committal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933#sec-53-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53(4) Indictable offences",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where a person has been committed for trial upon a charge for an\nindictable offence triable before the Supreme Court, the\ninformation against the person may include, either in substitution\nfor, or in addition to, a count charging the offence for which he\nwas committed, a count founded on a fact or evidence disclosed in\nthe course of the committal proceedings."
    },
    {
